  "verdict": "Spearman rho between a feature's a-priori correlated-electron association and how much its attribution is suppressed under DANN relative to a plain network is -0.094 (p=0.283). Mean suppression for the top-15 most correlated-electron-associated features is -0.00078 vs 0.00043 for the bottom-15 (least-associated, control) features. This does not clearly support the manuscript's inference of differential suppression: the top correlated-electron-associated features are not suppressed more than the control set under DANN by this measure. The domain-invariance objective appears to suppress broadly across the feature set rather than selectively targeting correlated-electron features, or the suppression signal is present but this attribution method is too noisy at this scale to detect it."
}